      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestions!\nReworked as suggested, and the dedicated worker thread is gone.\n\naddEntry() now runs on the logging thread this command already had,\nahead of the lg2::commit() call, and the record ID comes back through a\nstd::promise that is set as soon as the ID is assigned, before flush()\nwrites the file.\n\nselDataObj still needs a lock. With addEntry() on the logging thread,\nseveral of those can be in flight at once, so a mutex guards it and\nevery accessor takes it. I am holding it across flush() as well, which\nkeeps the file writes serialized and in entry order.",
